DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260515T193000
SUMMARY:Olafur Eliasson: Presence — GOMA Friday Nights
DESCRIPTION:Step into Olafur Eliasson's immersive multi-sensory art install
 ations during GOMA's special Friday night openings. The evening combines g
 allery access with bespoke bars\, live DJs\, pop-up performances\, and del
 icious bites — creating an artistically alive\, social atmosphere where ar
 t\, music\, and conversation naturally blend.
LOCATION:Gallery of Modern Art (GOMA)\, South Brisbane
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/event/goma-friday-nights-presence-2026-05
 -08
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260511
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260511
SUMMARY:Anywhere Festival — Week 3 (Multiple Venues)
DESCRIPTION:Brisbane's experimental arts festival uses hidden backyards\, f
 erries\, driveways\, and unexpected corners as stages. Week 3 features the
 atre in hedge mazes\, circus in driveways\, music in backyards\, immersive
  experiences\, and storytelling — hundreds of shows from emerging and esta
 blished artists across non-traditional venues.
LOCATION:Multiple Brisbane venues (Albion\, Yeronga\, Grange\, Milton\, Wes
 t End\, New Farm\, Fortitude Valley\, etc.)
URL:https://anywhere.is/brisbane/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-2@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260511T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260511T203000
SUMMARY:BrisScience: 'The Heat Is On — Growing Food in a Warmer World'
DESCRIPTION:UQ's monthly BrisScience lecture series brings science out of t
 he lab to the public. Dr Millicent Smith\, Senior Lecturer in Crop Physiol
 ogy\, explores how we can grow enough food in a warming world using cuttin
 g-edge phenotyping tools and novel crop diversity. Accessible to all\; no 
 prior knowledge required.
LOCATION:The Edge\, State Library of Queensland\, South Brisbane
URL:https://science.uq.edu.au/event/brisscience
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-3@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260515T170000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260515T190000
SUMMARY:Bands in Parks: Twilight Jazz by the River
DESCRIPTION:Free outdoor jazz performance by UQ Big Band at a beautiful riv
 erside park near the Goodwill Bridge. Watch the sunset over the Brisbane R
 iver with fellow music lovers in an informal\, social setting. Register vi
 a Eventbrite.
LOCATION:Queensland Maritime Museum Park\, South Brisbane
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com.au/e/bands-in-parks-twilight-jazz-by-the-riv
 er-tickets-1982143891738
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-5@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260514
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260514
SUMMARY:Free Range 6: SCRAPS (Laura Hill) @ IMA
DESCRIPTION:IMA's Free Range sound club features Laura Hill's SCRAPS — a 20
 -year Brisbane underground veteran's analogue synth-pop project blending c
 lub beats with keyboard pop. Intimate\, experimental\, and musically adven
 turous.
LOCATION:Institute of Modern Art\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://www.ima.org.au/ima-events/free-range-6/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-7@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260719
SUMMARY:'Make A Scene' — Queensland Museum Free Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Immersive free exhibition celebrating 1990s Australian queer cu
 lture — 35 years after decriminalisation of homosexuality. Features fashio
 n\, colour\, camp\, pop culture\, and personal stories from Brisbane's und
 erground nightclub and dance party scene. Culturally significant and histo
 rically rich.
LOCATION:Queensland Museum Kurilpa\, South Brisbane
URL:https://www.museum.qld.gov.au/kurilpa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-9@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260512T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260512T210000
SUMMARY:Mariah the Scientist: Hearts Sold Separately Tour
DESCRIPTION:Atlanta R&B and neo-soul artist Mariah the Scientist brings her
  emotionally intense\, atmospheric sound to Brisbane. A thoughtful\, artis
 tically ambitious performer with a devoted following among music lovers.
LOCATION:The Fortitude Music Hall\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://www.thefortitude.com.au/all-events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-10@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260515T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260515T210000
SUMMARY:J.I.D — God Does Like World Tour
DESCRIPTION:Atlanta rapper J.I.D (relocated from Riverstage) is one of hip-
 hop's most compelling live performers. Intimate headline show in a dedicat
 ed music venue rather than a large stadium.
LOCATION:The Fortitude Music Hall\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://www.thefortitude.com.au/all-events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-11@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260517T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260517T210000
SUMMARY:Genesis Owusu
DESCRIPTION:Ghanaian-Australian alt-soul and punk-funk artist Genesis Owusu
  is one of Australia's most electrifying live performers. Expect an intens
 e\, genre-defying show full of energy and artistic ambition.
LOCATION:The Fortitude Music Hall\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://www.thefortitude.com.au/all-events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-12@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T210000
SUMMARY:Audrey Hobert — The Staircase To Stardom Tour
DESCRIPTION:Rising indie-pop singer-songwriter Audrey Hobert brings her cin
 ematic\, emotionally rich songwriting to Brisbane. Intimate\, atmospheric 
 gig in a dedicated music venue.
LOCATION:The Fortitude Music Hall\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://www.thefortitude.com.au/all-events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-13@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260514T193000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260514T213000
SUMMARY:Jason Leong: In Laughing Memory
DESCRIPTION:Malaysian stand-up comedian Jason Leong brings sharp\, observat
 ional humour to Brisbane in an intimate touring comedy show.
LOCATION:The Fortitude Music Hall\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://www.thefortitude.com.au/all-events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-14@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260517
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260517
SUMMARY:Black Bear Lodge — Live Music & Sunday Service
DESCRIPTION:Brisbane's favourite live music venue curates first dibs on tou
 ring acts and intimate EP sets. Sunday Service features free live performa
 nces from Queensland's best emerging acts — a casual\, social vibe with mu
 sicians and music lovers.
LOCATION:Black Bear Lodge\, Fortitude Valley
URL:https://blackbearlodge.bar/events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-15@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260515T193000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260515T213000
SUMMARY:QSO Concert Special: The Italian Job
DESCRIPTION:Queensland Symphony Orchestra performs an Italian-themed progra
 m featuring Rossini\, Rota\, Verdi\, and Vivaldi arrangements. A celebrato
 ry orchestral evening by one of Australia's leading orchestras.
LOCATION:QPAC Concert Hall\, South Brisbane
URL:https://qso.com.au/events/2026/concert-specials-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-16@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T103000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T123000
SUMMARY:Weaving is Healing Brisbane
DESCRIPTION:Figure-8 coil weave workshop with roots in African and European
  traditions. Participants weave a small basket in a ceremony-style immersi
 ve sharing and healing circle. Hands-on\, creative\, and community-oriente
 d in a beautiful outdoor botanical setting.
LOCATION:Mt Coot-tha Botanic Gardens
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com.au/e/weaving-is-healing-brisbane-may-2026-ti
 ckets-1984547702601
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-17@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260511T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260511T200000
SUMMARY:Brisbane Makerspace — Monday Open Night
DESCRIPTION:Free public open night at Brisbane's community makerspace. Acce
 ss to laser cutting\, 3D printing\, electronics\, and arts & crafts tools.
  Recurring event to meet makers\, learn\, and collaborate — no membership 
 required for public meetups.
LOCATION:Brisbane Makerspace\, Fortitude Valley area
URL:https://brisbanemaker.space/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-20@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260513
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260513
SUMMARY:Avid Reader Open Book Club
DESCRIPTION:Avid Reader's Open Book Club is the first Wednesday evening or 
 Thursday morning of each month — ideal for newcomers. Recurring community 
 of readers and thoughtful people. The bookshop also hosts author talks and
  runs themed clubs (Bloody Crime\, Young & Restless\, Australian literatur
 e).
LOCATION:Avid Reader\, West End
URL:https://www.avidreader.com.au/events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-21@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260515
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260515
SUMMARY:Brisbane Language Exchange — Friday Social
DESCRIPTION:Weekly casual gathering for people who want to practice foreign
  languages and meet curious\, internationally-minded locals and expats. Na
 tural conversation opportunity in a social\, relaxed setting.
LOCATION:Brisbane City (check Eventbrite for venue)
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com.au/d/australia/brisbane/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-22@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260515
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260515
SUMMARY:Redlands Coast AdventureFest
DESCRIPTION:10-day festival showcasing adventure activities and outdoor eve
 nts across Redlands Coast — hiking\, nature excursions\, coastal activitie
 s\, and community events. Ideal for adventurous\, active social types and 
 nature lovers.
LOCATION:Redlands Coast (approx. 30–40 mins from Brisbane CBD)
URL:https://www.mustdobrisbane.com/whats-on
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-23@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T090000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T110000
SUMMARY:Dog Lovers Festival Brisbane 2026
DESCRIPTION:Queensland's biggest dog celebration returns. Hundreds of dogs\
 , breed showcases\, adoption zones\, and a family-friendly\, joyful commun
 ity atmosphere. Unexpectedly warm and social — a place to meet fellow anim
 al lovers and their furry companions.
LOCATION:Brisbane Showgrounds\, Bowen Hills
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com.au/d/australia/brisbane/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-26@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260514T193000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260514T213000
SUMMARY:ADFAS Lecture: 'The World's Greatest Paintings — 200 Years of the N
 ational Gallery'
DESCRIPTION:Lecturer Simon Whitehouse explores the National Gallery's 200-y
 ear history (1824–present)\, including early suffragette sabotage\, bombs\
 , theft\, and the story of the original 'Angerstein 38' paintings. Intelle
 ctually engaging art history lecture for curious audiences.
LOCATION:Royal Queensland Art Society (Wed) / State Library of Queensland A
 uditorium 1 (Thu)
URL:https://www.artsnational.au/societies/brisbane/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-27@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T083000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260516T103000
SUMMARY:Kids Tour: Presence & Play (Family Art Tour @ GOMA)
DESCRIPTION:Multi-sensory art tour of Olafur Eliasson's Presence designed f
 or families with children. Guided through playful experiences that spark i
 magination and build connection\, followed by exclusive crowd-free exhibit
 ion viewing.
LOCATION:Gallery of Modern Art (GOMA)\, South Brisbane
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/event/kids-tours-presence-and-play-2026-0
 7-04
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-28@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260511T083000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260511T103000
SUMMARY:Inspiring Future Skills Symposium 2026 — Brisbane
DESCRIPTION:Teacher-focused (but open to anyone interested in technology an
 d education) professional learning on embedding future skills — AI\, big d
 ata\, quantum computing\, robotics\, augmented reality — into teaching and
  learning. Brings together education leaders\, curriculum innovators\, and
  industry experts.
LOCATION:QUT Kelvin Grove Campus\, Kelvin Grove
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com.au/e/inspiring-future-skills-symposium-2026-
 brisbane-tickets-1983053099202
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-29@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260514T210000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260514T230000
SUMMARY:Vertigo Rooftop Dining — Brisbane Powerhouse
DESCRIPTION:High-adventure dining experience: guests don safety harnesses\,
  climb to rooftop seats with 17-metre drops beneath them\, and enjoy a loc
 ally sourced meal from Bar Alto. Option to descend via rope dropline down 
 the building's façade. Uniquely Brisbane and genuinely memorable.
LOCATION:Brisbane Powerhouse Rooftop\, New Farm
URL:https://brisbanepowerhouse.org/neighbourhood/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-30@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260501
SUMMARY:Double Take — Australian Cinémathèque Film Program
DESCRIPTION:Curated cinema program at GOMA's Cinémathèque — a fixture for f
 ilm lovers seeking thoughtful\, artistically selected screenings in an int
 imate gallery cinema setting.
LOCATION:Australian Cinémathèque\, Gallery of Modern Art\, South Brisbane
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/stories/top-5-things-to-see-and-do-at-qag
 oma-in-may-2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-31@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260524
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260524
SUMMARY:MJ The Musical
DESCRIPTION:Olivier and four-time Tony Award-winning musical set in 1992\, 
 offering a behind-the-scenes look at Michael Jackson's Dangerous World Tou
 r creation through an MTV journalist's lens. Genuinely spectacular live pe
 rformance experience.
LOCATION:Lyric Theatre\, QPAC\, South Brisbane
URL:https://www.qpac.com.au
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-32@dothings
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260424
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260424
SUMMARY:Brisbane Comedy Festival — Multiple Shows
DESCRIPTION:City-wide comedy festival featuring bold solo shows\, late-nigh
 t performances\, and genre-bending acts — from satire and silliness to big
 -hearted storytelling. Browse individual shows for intimate solo performan
 ces at smaller venues.
LOCATION:Brisbane Powerhouse (New Farm)\, The Tivoli\, Fortitude Music Hall
 \, The Princess Theatre (Woolloongabba)
URL:https://www.brisbanecomedyfestival.com.au
